---
description: VibeRaven always-on architecture, release, and provider context for agents
alwaysApply: true
---

At the start of real app work, map the architecture boundary before editing: UI/API, auth/session, data/schema/RLS, provider dashboard, deploy/env, background job/webhook, billing, storage, or release/version drift.

Ask concise questions only when the answer changes the plan: last working version, production symptom, provider involved, deploy target, or provider/dashboard proof.

Open Studio with `npx -y viberaven` for context. Run `npx -y viberaven --agent-mode` before deploy, provider-sensitive, database-policy, or dependency changes when artifact context is needed.

Read `.viberaven/agent-tasklist.md` first, then `.viberaven/gate-result.json` and `.viberaven/mission-map.md`.
Fix one scoped gap, then `npx -y viberaven --verify`. Before CI or production promote: `npx -y viberaven --strict`.

Context is not clear until the architecture boundary, release/version context, and provider proof boundary are understood. For launch gates, `gate.status === "clear"` is required.

Before editing these files, read `.viberaven/agent-context.md` and `.viberaven/mission-map.md` for what changed, which architecture boundary is affected, and which provider context matters.

Full VibeRaven rules: `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` (installed by `npx -y viberaven init --agents all`).